Based on the provided code and CVE-2023-44466 details, the vulnerability stems from an **integer signedness error** in the `ceph_decode_32` function when handling untrusted length fields from TCP packets. Here's what the patch does to fix the issue:

## Root Cause
The `decode_preamble` function uses `ceph_decode_32(&p)` to read segment lengths from untrusted network data:
```c
for (i = 0; i < desc->fd_seg_cnt; i++) {
    desc->fd_lens[i] = ceph_decode_32(&p);  // Vulnerable line
    desc->fd_aligns[i] = ceph_decode_16(&p);
