    pr_err("control segment too big %d\n", desc->fd_lens[0]);
    return -EINVAL;
}
```

## The Fix
The patch adds **explicit checks for negative values** before the existing bounds validation:

```c
for (i = 0; i < desc->fd_seg_cnt; i++) {
    desc->fd_lens[i] = ceph_decode_32(&p);
    desc->fd_aligns[i] = ceph_decode_16(&p);

    // NEW: Check for negative lengths
    if (desc->fd_lens[i] < 0) {
        pr_err("negative segment length %d\n", desc->fd_lens[i]);
        return -EINVAL;
    }
}
```

This prevents the integer signedness error from bypassing bounds checks and causing buffer overflows when the negative values are later used in memory allocation or buffer operations.

The patch ensures that malformed HELLO or AUTH frames with crafted negative length fields are properly rejected, preventing potential remote code execution.

