This function is responsible for walking through hugetlb (huge page) ranges in the Linux kernel's memory management subsystem. According to CVE-2017-16994, the vulnerability exists because `walk_hugetlb_range` improperly handles holes in hugetlb ranges, which allows local users to potentially read uninitialized kernel memory via a specially crafted `mincore()` system call.

