The most common approach is to ensure proper cleanup by moving the `finish_wait()` call to occur in all code paths where `prepare_to_wait()` was executed, preventing the wait queue corruption that leads to the kernel crash.

This fix ensures that even when the SQ polling thread is marked as dead (`ctx->sqo_dead = 1`), the wait queue is properly cleaned up, eliminating the use-after-free vulnerability.

