- Rate limiting on route additions from the same source
- Maximum route table size enforcement
- Proper cleanup of temporary/duplicate routes

This allows remote attackers on the same network segment to cause denial-of-service through memory exhaustion, as the system continuously allocates memory for route entries until resources are depleted.

