    return -1;
```

This validation prevents:
1. **Integer underflow** when `l < 10` (which would cause `l - 10` to underflow)
2. **Buffer overflow** when `l > 20` (which would cause excessive data to be copied into the `callsign` buffer)

The patch ensures that the length field `l` is within safe bounds before performing memory operations that depend on `l - 10`.

